### Variables
@gateway = http://localhost:8080

### ─── AUTH ───────────────────────────────────────────

### Register new customer account
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Alice Uwase",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "phone": "0781234567",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Login (copy the token from the response into @token below)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Set token after login (paste your token here)
@token = paste_your_token_here

### ─── CUSTOMERS ─────────────────────────────────────

### Create customer
POST {{gateway}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Uwase",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "phone": "0781234567"
}

### Get all customers
GET {{gateway}}/api/customers

### Get customer by ID
GET {{gateway}}/api/customers/1

### Delete customer
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/customers/1

### ─── RESTAURANTS ────────────────────────────────────

### Create restaurant
POST {{gateway}}/api/restaurants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pizza Palace",
  "address": "KN 5 Ave, Kigali",
  "cuisineType": "Italian"
}

### Get all restaurants
GET {{gateway}}/api/restaurants

### Get restaurant by ID
GET {{gateway}}/api/restaurants/1

### Delete restaurant
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/restaurants/1

### ─── ORDERS ─────────────────────────────────────────

### Create order
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "restaurantId": 1,
  "totalAmount": 25.99
}

### Get all orders
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders

### Get order by ID
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/1

### Delete order
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/orders/1

### ─── CIRCUIT BREAKER TESTS ─────────────────────────
# HOW TO TEST:
# 1. Run the happy-path requests below (services UP) — expect 200/201
# 2. Stop customer-service:  docker stop food-delivery-customer-service
# 3. Run the "service DOWN" requests — expect fallback error message, NOT a timeout
# 4. Check circuit state in actuator (requests below)
# 5. Restart:  docker start food-delivery-customer-service

### [HAPPY PATH] Place order — customer-service and restaurant-service both UP
# Expected: 201 with order object and delivery auto-created via RabbitMQ
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/place
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 5,
  "restaurantId": 2,
  "totalAmount": 25.99
}

###

### [CIRCUIT BREAKER] Place order — stop customer-service first
# docker stop food-delivery-customer-service
# Expected: 500 with "Customer service is unavailable" message (NOT a 30s timeout)
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/place
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 5,
  "restaurantId": 2,
  "totalAmount": 25.99
}

###

### [CIRCUIT BREAKER] Place order — stop restaurant-service first
# docker stop food-delivery-restaurant-service
# Expected: 500 with "Restaurant service is unavailable" message
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/place
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "restaurantId": 1,
  "totalAmount": 25.99
}

###

### Check circuit breaker state — order-service (customer-service circuit)
# Expected: shows CLOSED (normal), OPEN (tripped), or HALF_OPEN (recovering)
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/circuitbreakers

###

### Check circuit breaker state — delivery-service (order-service circuit)
GET http://localhost:8084/actuator/circuitbreakers

###

### Check circuit breaker health — order-service
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health

###

